# Deploy NAS Gestiio — tar+base64 + finish soft (default)

Target: `Carmine@192.168.1.50` · app path `/home/Carmine/apps/gestiio-20260624-2128` · container `gestiio-app`

## Trasporto file: tar + base64 (preferito)

Su Windows **non usare `scp` diretto**. Usare **Git Bash**:

```powershell
& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc 'cd /c/Users/carva/Desktop/Progetti/gestiio && sh ops/deploy-*.sh'
```

```sh
HOST="Carmine@192.168.1.50"
APP="/home/Carmine/apps/gestiio-20260624-2128"
DOCKER="/Volume1/@apps/DockerEngine/dockerd/bin/docker"
CONTAINER="gestiio-app"

tar -cf /tmp/gestiio-<nome>.tar path/to/file1 ...
base64 /tmp/gestiio-<nome>.tar | ssh "$HOST" "base64 -d > /tmp/gestiio-<nome>.tar"
ssh "$HOST" "
set -e
cd $APP
tar -xf /tmp/gestiio-<nome>.tar
$DOCKER cp $APP/path/file $CONTAINER:/var/www/html/path/file
# finish soft (sotto)
"
rm -f /tmp/gestiio-<nome>.tar
```

## Finish soft (DEFAULT — Blade / CSS / JS / PHP)

**Non** fare `cache:clear` + `optimize:clear` + `docker restart` su ogni deploy UI:
dopo il restart OPcache è vuoto e `/backend` resta a 15–30s per diversi refresh.

```sh
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'rm -rf /var/www/html/storage/framework/views/*; php /var/www/html/artisan view:clear'
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'php /var/www/html/artisan config:cache; php /var/www/html/artisan route:cache; php /var/www/html/artisan view:cache' || true
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'php -r "if (function_exists(\"opcache_reset\")) { opcache_reset(); }"' || true
# Preserva app cache; riscalda solo il marker giornaliero
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'php /var/www/html/artisan tinker --execute="Illuminate\\Support\\Facades\\Cache::put(\"CacheUnaVoltaAlGiorno\", now(), now()->endOfDay());"' || true
```

Per asset sotto `assets_backend/`: copiare anche in `public/assets_backend/` se DocumentRoot è `public/`.

Verifica marker (`grep`) sui file nel container. **Restart solo se** cambia `.env`, Apache/PHP ini, o OPcache non rilascia proprio il PHP.

Template: `ops/_deploy-finish-soft.sh`

## Finish hard (solo se necessario)

Usare **solo** per migrate/composer/.env/opcache sticky:

```sh
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'rm -rf /var/www/html/storage/framework/views/*; php /var/www/html/artisan view:clear; php /var/www/html/artisan config:cache; php /var/www/html/artisan route:cache; php /var/www/html/artisan view:cache'
# NON cache:clear a meno che non sia obbligatorio
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'php -r "if (function_exists(\"opcache_reset\")) { opcache_reset(); }"' || true
$DOCKER restart $CONTAINER
sleep 8
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'php /var/www/html/artisan tinker --execute="Illuminate\\Support\\Facades\\Cache::put(\"CacheUnaVoltaAlGiorno\", now(), now()->endOfDay());"' || true
$DOCKER exec $CONTAINER sh -lc 'curl -sk -o /dev/null http://127.0.0.1/login; curl -sk -o /dev/null http://127.0.0.1/login'
```

